WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.100
Nikhil: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.510
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:06.330
between Dunkin' Donuts
in India and in the US.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:08.247
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:13.920
Here in the US, you can get your doughnuts

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:17.010
in one; six, or a half dozen;

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.520
or 12, aka a dozen.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.260
Don't put that in there.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.820
Here in India, you can get your doughnuts

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:27.840
in packs of one, three, or six.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:31.770
One US sticky glazed doughnut.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:32.910
Nikhil: Indian glazed doughnut.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.770
Joe: It weighs ...

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:35.869
Nikhil: 49 grams.

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:37.530
Joe: 59 grams.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:40.590
In the US, we have four
sizes of hot coffee.

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.680
The small, the medium, the large,

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.630
which, unfortunately, they forgot.

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:47.550
Dunkin'!

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:49.320
And the extra large.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:50.880
Here in India, our filter coffee

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.610
comes in one size, this one.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:55.140
If you're wondering what filter coffee is,

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.900
it's one of the most popular
drinks here in India.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.300
It's made by taking a decoction of coffee,

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.462
mixing it with sweetened milk,

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:03.990
and typically when they're preparing it,

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:07.410
they pour it from a huge
height to create this froth.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:09.900
It's super delicious,
and it's very strong.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.550
It'll wake you right up in the morning.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.740
As for our other drinks,
they come in two sizes.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.080
Either medium or large.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.520
This is an Americano.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.100
Let's weigh it to see how much we got.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.830
I might have to go to
the bathroom after this.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:25.830
10.14 fluid ounces.

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:27.300
If that's not enough for you,

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:30.360
Dunkin's in the US also has a Box 'O Joe,

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.990
which contains 100 ounces of hot coffee.

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:35.316
And ...

00:01:35.316 --> 00:01:36.565
[groaning]

00:01:36.565 --> 00:01:38.161
Guzh!

00:01:38.161 --> 00:01:39.144
Oh, yeah.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:42.270
Oh, yeah.

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:43.890
This should be the extra large.

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:47.610
In the US, we "only" have
three iced-coffee sizes.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:49.860
The small, the medium, and the large.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:52.070
No extra large, but they did remember

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:54.210
the large iced coffee,
so, thanks, Dunkin'.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:55.950
So, the Dunkin' India website says

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:57.270
that they serve an iced Americano.

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:00.090
But we asked three
outlets here in Bengaluru,

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:01.920
and they said no iced Americano.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:02.753
We even asked them,

00:02:02.753 --> 00:02:04.537
"Hey, can you put some
ice in our Americano?"

00:02:04.537 --> 00:02:05.370
They said no.

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:07.617
So if you really must have an Americano

00:02:07.617 --> 00:02:09.866
that's iced from Dunkin',

00:02:09.866 --> 00:02:11.674
you have to take your
own ice and go there.

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:17.448
So, what's the large?

00:02:17.448 --> 00:02:18.570
Is this supposed to be 32?

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:19.680
I mean, I think it's --

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:22.112
Yeah, cup says 32, it's supposed to be 32.

00:02:22.112 --> 00:02:25.770
Yuelei, zoom in on that
and shame this business!

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:27.308
32?

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:30.810
This is everything that
you'll find on the menu

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:33.960
at Dunkin' Donuts India that
you will not find in the US.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:36.660
Here is everything you can
get in a US Dunkin' Donuts

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:38.610
you can't get in India.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:42.510
Let's start off with this
one. It is called Choco Villa.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:43.440
And I think it's called that

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.270
because there's a little
triangle of chocolate,

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:47.970
which looks like those houses
we used to draw as kids.

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:52.290
Oh, my God.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:53.550
Yum!

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:56.250
It's filled with my favorite
doughnut filling ever,

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:58.010
which is Bavarian cream.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:02:59.583
Choco almond.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.380
Hm, it's OK.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:06.480
It's filled with the Bavarian cream again.

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:11.370
With the cream, unreal.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:14.070
On to the next one. This
is called a Chocoholic.

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:17.310
It's got a piece of KitKat
sticking through it.

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:19.621
I want to see if it's one KitKat
bar or if they've taken two

00:03:19.621 --> 00:03:21.420
and they've sandwiched them together.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:22.920
Let's pull from this end.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.633
Yeah, I was right.

00:03:26.884 --> 00:03:29.430
If you're a chocoholic,
this is the one for you.

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:33.060
The inside has also got
chocolaty filling in there.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.330
Chocolate is starting to
hit me real hard right now.

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:38.010
This stuff is so sweet.

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:40.210
This is called Rainbow Crunch.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:43.553
Oh.

00:03:43.553 --> 00:03:46.260
There's strawberry frosting on top.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.600
So this has a strawberry taste.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.490
It's OK. It's a doughnut.

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:52.680
Next up, we have Cookie Delight.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:53.708
It's called Cookie Delight

00:03:53.708 --> 00:03:56.760
'cause they've taken cookie
powder and smacked it on top.

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.350
This one's called Crispy Crunch.

00:03:58.350 --> 00:04:00.600
For people who have trypophobia,

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:02.433
this one is probably not for you.

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:06.870
Oh, my God, this ain't it.

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:09.450
The crispy stuff on top
is just not working.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:12.150
Again, however, they do have
the Bavarian cream inside --

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:16.380
I feel like there's a hurricane
inside my body right now.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.740
Next up, we have a
doughnut called the Gemmy.

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:23.340
My fellow Indians will recognize
that there are gems on top.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:26.880
This is one of the most nostalgic
chocolates here in India,

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:28.983
and I've eaten them since I was a kid.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:31.193
Super yum.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.000
You'd think a kid would like them,

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.490
but I can't even imagine
a kid version of myself

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:40.440
liking something that's so overdosed

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:41.880
with sweetness and chocolate.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.560
Is it Gemmy? Yes.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.570
Too Gemmy? Also yes.

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:46.530
I'd avoid.

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:48.960
So, I thought this was all
the exclusive signatures,

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.390
but I've been told that
there are two more.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:54.270
And let's start off with this
one. It's called Choco Pop.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.400
It's got chocolate on
top, chocolate sprinkles,

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:59.430
chocolate wavy line things,
and it's filled with chocolate.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:00.546
It's very sweet.

00:05:05.118 --> 00:05:06.285
Ah.

00:05:08.661 --> 00:05:10.427
Whew!

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:20.340
All right.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:21.630
And on to our last doughnut.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:24.393
This one is called the Choco Berry Bomb.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:28.770
That's actually quite nice.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:31.950
It has definitely cut the
sweetness that I've experienced.

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:34.770
There's, like, some berry jam inside,

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:36.960
which is kind of tart and nice.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:40.380
The top is milk chocolate with
shavings of white chocolate.

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:41.213
Whew!

00:05:41.213 --> 00:05:42.870
Yeah, it's a good doughnut.

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:44.640
I wouldn't order it. It's too much.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:46.320
All of this, I would
not order any of these.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:47.400
They're too much.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.629
Exclusive doughnuts you can get in the US

00:05:49.629 --> 00:05:51.570
you can't get in India.

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:54.660
Now, we're filming this
the first week of October.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:57.852
Of course, the No. 1 flavor
you get this month is pumpkin.

00:05:59.602 --> 00:06:01.530
Mm, so pumpkiny.

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:03.270
Yeah, this tastes just like pumpkin pie.

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:06.270
Also, you can get yourself
a glazed blueberry doughnut.

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:07.260
See? Look at that.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:10.410
Glaze on top, blueberry
dough on the inside.

00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:12.390
Also delicious. Love it.

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:16.293
Glazed chocolate. Figured
this was everywhere, right?

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:19.073
So good.

00:06:19.073 --> 00:06:20.760
Ooh, Boston cream.

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:22.350
The Ben Affleck of doughnuts.

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:23.400
Looks like a regular doughnut,

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:24.749
doesn't it, everyone in India?

00:06:24.749 --> 00:06:25.982
But

00:06:27.115 --> 00:06:29.881
surprise, there's cream on the inside!

00:06:29.881 --> 00:06:30.810
I know everyone likes doughnuts,

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:31.710
maybe I haven't had a doughnut in a while,

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:33.600
but crap, this is really good.

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:34.710
One of my favorites.

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:35.760
I f--- with these.

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:37.860
Double chocolate, maybe my favorite,

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:39.480
'cause they just did what they had to do.

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:41.760
Take a chocolate doughnut and
put that chocolate frosting

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:44.700
I like right on top of
it. A double threat.

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:45.933
Oh, these are so good.

00:06:48.154 --> 00:06:50.533
I am in heaven!

00:06:50.533 --> 00:06:53.880
A strawberry frosting with sprinkles?

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:55.230
You don't got this?

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:57.300
This is, like, the Homer
Simpson doughnut, right?

00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:59.640
This is the one that you
always see him eating.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:01.440
Oh, the vanilla cream.

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:03.401
Gotta say, don't think I've
ever had this one before.

00:07:06.622 --> 00:07:07.705
Look at me.

00:07:07.705 --> 00:07:09.960
It's like "Scarface" over
here. I'm just covered.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:10.957
A little much.

00:07:10.957 --> 00:07:12.292
Ugh! Ugh!

00:07:12.292 --> 00:07:13.375
Oh, God.

00:07:13.375 --> 00:07:15.570
Here's some powder right here.

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:16.590
Powdered doughnut.

00:07:16.590 --> 00:07:18.030
India, you don't know what this is?

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:19.997
C'mon. It's, like, doughnut No. 1, right?

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:25.050
Also in the US you can get a
vanilla frosted with sprinkles,

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:27.840
and a bear claw, which they
unfortunately did not have

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:29.080
at the time of shooting this.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:31.260
Anyway, ah.

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:33.885
Munchkins? You guys don't got Munchkins?

00:07:33.885 --> 00:07:35.280
What?

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:36.990
We have a variety of Munchkin flavors,

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:40.856
but this one specifically
is the pumpkin Munchkin,

00:07:40.856 --> 00:07:42.747
and,

00:07:42.747 --> 00:07:44.064
mm!

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:47.640
Tastes just like pumpkin pie. Fantastic.

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:50.250
Hey, guys, we're now on to a
different category of doughnuts

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:52.170
called the all-time favorites.

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:55.200
I took a quick hospital visit,
and I'm completely fine now.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:57.050
I'm sorry about the madness

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:59.683
from the previous set of doughnuts.

00:07:59.683 --> 00:08:02.430
I'm fine now. I don't
know what came over me.

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:05.820
OK, so we'll start off with
this specimen over here.

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:07.890
It's called a Cookie Cartwheel.

00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:10.530
Adorable name, and, yes,
it does look like a wheel.

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:12.665
I like how they put the white stripes.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.140
Yeah.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.460
It's sweet.

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:18.870
Next up on our list is a doughnut

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:20.160
that's not intimidating at all,

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:23.940
it's only called Death by Chocolate.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:25.440
Will this kill me?

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:26.460
Probably not.

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:29.670
But will this give me some
diabetes if I eat too much?

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:30.690
Absolutely.

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:33.030
And for that reason,
it's a win in my book.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:35.700
If you thought Death
by Chocolate was scary,

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.740
this is Alive by Chocolate.

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:39.630
In terms of visual
differences, I can already tell

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:42.150
this one has more of a
cookie crumble on top.

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:44.730
They're very similar, as expected.

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:48.000
I will say, this one, it feels more, like,

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:51.420
it lifts your spirits
and you feel more alive.

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:55.260
And this one will probably
put you to sleep, in a coma.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:57.509
So death and alive, it makes sense.

00:08:57.509 --> 00:09:01.984
[ears ringing]

00:09:03.705 --> 00:09:05.438
Mm, whoa!

00:09:05.438 --> 00:09:08.340
On to the next one. We
have something called

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:11.010
Very Very Strawberry.

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:13.770
Vanilla frosting on top,
it's got some pink streaks,

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:16.920
and it looks to be stuffed
with strawberry jam.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:17.910
Which sounds amazing,

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:20.223
especially after all
this chocolate overdose.

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:24.315
It's sweet.

00:09:24.315 --> 00:09:25.590
Oh, my God.

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:26.790
It's nice, though.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:29.010
All right, it's time
for our final doughnut,

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:32.610
and this one is a bit of a boss battle.

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:33.900
So, this is a doughnut eclair.

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:37.080
It's called the Breakup Party Eclair.

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:40.320
I guess because if you
go through a breakup,

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:41.780
this is what you end up eating.

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:48.060
So, the first few bites were quite nice.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:51.300
They weren't as sweet, and
they didn't feel as rich.

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:53.840
But I realized most of the
chocolate is kind of centered

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:56.610
towards the center of the eclair.

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:59.340
And so it's a lot more
decadent the closer you get.

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:02.730
Great for breakups, great as
a metaphor for what you feel

00:10:02.730 --> 00:10:04.140
when you're going through a breakup,

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:06.960
and as a doughnut itself, pretty average.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:10.110
Both hot and cold espresso
and coffee drinks in the US

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:13.050
have options for flavors
you can add as flavor shots,

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:14.100
which are unsweetened,

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:16.530
or flavor swirls, which
are sweet and creamy.

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:20.640
Now, flavors unique to
the US include shots of

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:23.673
vanilla, toasted almond, blueberry,

00:10:23.673 --> 00:10:25.860
raspberry, and coconut.

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:28.510
And flavor swirls, you can get

00:10:28.510 --> 00:10:30.593
French vanilla and pumpkin.

00:10:30.593 --> 00:10:34.920
So, I went ahead and had each
one of those swirls and shots

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:37.650
added to one coffee,
right here in front of me.

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:40.500
We'll call it the Food Wars DrinkAroo.

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:41.940
I don't know what it is.

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:44.310
All the flavors in one drink.

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:46.980
The lady when I ordered
it was like, "Really?"

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:48.650
And I was like, "Really."

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:53.533
Oh, God, this is so bad.

00:10:53.533 --> 00:10:54.709
Oh, ugh!

00:10:54.709 --> 00:10:56.460
Just blegh. Whoa!

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:57.650
Oh, man.

00:10:58.596 --> 00:10:59.880
[exhales sharply]

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:01.648
It's like, there's, like,
an electric charge to it

00:11:01.648 --> 00:11:03.440
at the end I don't quite understand.

00:11:05.386 --> 00:11:06.636
Mm.

00:11:06.636 --> 00:11:08.340
Oh-ho-ho-ho-ho!

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:10.250
This is poison. Don't get it.

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:11.340
All right, it's time for drinks.

00:11:11.340 --> 00:11:13.200
Let's start off with the cold options

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:15.180
that we have here at Dunkin' India.

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:17.550
The first one is a classic lemonade.

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:18.600
Let's go ahead and try it.

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:19.863
It looks very clear.

00:11:21.211 --> 00:11:22.350
That was nice. Refreshing.

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:24.750
They have not made it too
sweet, and I kind of like it.

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:26.801
Next up, we have a virgin mojito.

00:11:30.150 --> 00:11:33.360
I don't see why somebody
would go to Dunkin' Donuts,

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:37.200
get a doughnut, and then a
virgin mojito on the side.

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:39.540
Quick point to make: You can
get them in a small bottle,

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:42.090
or you can even get
them in larger options.

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:43.880
Next up, we have two flavors of iced tea.

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:46.593
We have lemon and peach.
I'm going to try the peach.

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:51.690
If I had to pick one of these,
this is the one I'd go for.

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:55.290
Exclusive hot drinks here in
the US, we have these three.

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:58.410
The first one is, like, a
specific coffee blend at Dunkin'

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:00.363
called Dunkin' Midnight.

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:05.670
Oh, wow, that has,
[stammers] that's strong.

00:12:05.670 --> 00:12:07.301
Wow.

00:12:07.301 --> 00:12:10.140
It's, like, really
strong. I kinda love it.

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:13.290
Moving on, you can get
yourself a chai latte.

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:16.170
India doesn't have chai
lattes? What's going on, guys?

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:17.280
That's really good.

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:18.990
And, of course, a matcha latte.

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:20.503
No, not matcha.

00:12:20.503 --> 00:12:21.960
I hate matcha.

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:23.340
That's the green one, right?

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:25.538
Beverages that taste like lawn clippings.

00:12:27.257 --> 00:12:29.141
Mm-mm.

00:12:29.141 --> 00:12:30.210
Ugh. I hate it.

00:12:30.210 --> 00:12:32.205
All right, it's now
time for our milk-based

00:12:32.205 --> 00:12:33.870
cold beverages here in India.

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:36.810
We have a range of frappés,
some iced shaken coffees.

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:38.070
Let's start with the frappés.

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:42.390
Coffee, caramel, and hazelnut.

00:12:42.390 --> 00:12:45.690
And they have a seasonal
flavor, which is Alphonso mango.

00:12:45.690 --> 00:12:48.300
If you've not heard of the
Alphonso variety of mangoes,

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:49.890
it grows all over here in India,

00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:52.110
and it is the king of mangoes.

00:12:52.110 --> 00:12:53.730
You have to try it if you get a chance.

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:54.690
I'm going to start off with this one,

00:12:54.690 --> 00:12:56.765
because I love mango-flavored anything.

00:12:58.890 --> 00:13:00.030
It's not bad.

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:03.090
Next up, we have some shaken iced coffees

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:06.828
in three flavors, caramel,
classic, and hazelnut.

00:13:06.828 --> 00:13:09.930
Also the classic flavored
shaken iced coffee,

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:14.160
it's not as sweet, and I want
to put this one on a pedestal.

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:16.020
Thank you.

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:19.920
OK, next up, they also sell a
iced mocha and an iced latte.

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:21.540
It's time for the chocolate milkshake,

00:13:21.540 --> 00:13:24.690
and can I just say, looks decadent.

00:13:24.690 --> 00:13:28.110
It's quite thick. It's kind of grainy.

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:30.780
Like, you can taste the
graininess of the chocolate,

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:32.610
which I like, but I don't know,

00:13:32.610 --> 00:13:34.110
some people might not like that.

00:13:34.110 --> 00:13:37.140
Some people might like really
smooth chocolate milkshakes.

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:38.490
OK, so if you're traveling to India

00:13:38.490 --> 00:13:40.800
and you must eat at Dunkin',
I would recommend you have

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:44.550
the Alphonso mango
frappé if it's in season.

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:47.160
But I would also say, don't go to Dunkin',

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:50.760
go to any juice shop, you'll
find them all across India,

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:51.990
and they take fresh mangoes,

00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:53.310
and they make you a mango milkshake

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:55.260
that will blow your mind.

00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:58.260
They'll put actual pieces
of Alphonso pulp in there,

00:13:58.260 --> 00:14:00.623
and you'll chew on it while
you drink your milkshake.

00:14:00.623 --> 00:14:01.523
Godsends.

00:14:01.523 --> 00:14:04.920
Joe: So, they made these
two hours ago. I'm sorry.

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:06.330
Assume they don't look like this.

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:08.190
Anyway, we have these
cold drinks in the US.

00:14:08.190 --> 00:14:09.120
They're called refreshers.

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:10.650
They're actually pretty
good, surprisingly.

00:14:10.650 --> 00:14:14.730
Starting down here, we have
the strawberry dragon fruit.

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:16.895
I am such a child. It's spelled

00:14:16.895 --> 00:14:21.803
S-T-R-A-W-D-R-G-N-F-R-T,

00:14:21.803 --> 00:14:24.003
and all I could think
of was "dragon fart."

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:26.760
Wow, that's actually pretty good.

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:28.232
Peach passion fruit.

00:14:28.232 --> 00:14:29.857
[laughing] F-R-T.

00:14:29.857 --> 00:14:32.127
I keep thinking "fart." I'm such a child.

00:14:32.127 --> 00:14:33.090
[fart tooting]

00:14:33.090 --> 00:14:35.760
Whoa! Blegh! What the hell?

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:37.920
I think all the syrup went to the bottom.

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:39.837
It's way stronger than it should be.

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:42.630
Yeah, 'cause up top it's really weak.

00:14:42.630 --> 00:14:44.640
Somewhere between there's a
good sip, but I didn't find it.

00:14:44.640 --> 00:14:45.900
Anyway, all right.

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:49.200
Peach passion fruit coconut.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:51.735
Oh, well this is -- is
that cool? Does that work?

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:56.430
OK.

00:14:56.430 --> 00:14:57.496
Ah, no.

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:01.860
Oh, gross. Yeah.

00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:04.020
The coconut ones are bad.

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:05.550
Keeping it up on the cool drinks,

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:07.590
you can get yourself a frozen coffee,

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:11.160
a frozen matcha latte, a frozen chocolate,

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:13.200
and, of course, the Coolattas.

00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:15.390
Wait, frozen hot chocolate?

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:16.940
Isn't that just chocolate milk?

00:15:18.648 --> 00:15:21.270
Oh, man, that is strong.

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:22.440
That is a milkshake.

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:23.343
Yo.

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:28.410
It's not terrible. The
flavor is very strong.

00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:31.350
This is apparently a blue raspberry.

00:15:31.350 --> 00:15:32.900
Think they have other flavors, but.

00:15:35.610 --> 00:15:38.610
Once upon a time, I
worked at a movie theater.

00:15:38.610 --> 00:15:39.600
Yes, really.

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:43.290
But we figured out a way
to get into the syrup box,

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:44.910
'cause fountain drinks,
it's syrup and soda water

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:46.682
at the same time, and it mixes
right when you pour it in.

00:15:46.682 --> 00:15:48.300
It was a really dark color,

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:49.650
and we dared each other to drink it.

00:15:49.650 --> 00:15:52.560
I remember it was so powerful,

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:54.480
I thought I was gonna throw up.

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:56.098
And I never experienced anything

00:15:56.098 --> 00:15:58.890
that powerful-flavored, until today.

00:15:58.890 --> 00:15:59.880
Surprise, surprise.

00:15:59.880 --> 00:16:02.490
Dunkin' Donuts also sells chai.

00:16:02.490 --> 00:16:04.830
So, you have two flavors,
this is ginger chai,

00:16:04.830 --> 00:16:06.810
and we have elaichi chai.

00:16:06.810 --> 00:16:10.320
Elaichi is cardamom.

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:12.243
Ginger in Hindi is adrak.

00:16:12.243 --> 00:16:14.679
And it's just such a beautiful
word to say, oh, my God!

00:16:14.679 --> 00:16:16.375
Adrak chai!

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:20.258
Oof, they've gone heavy
on the ginger for sure.

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:24.450
As advertised, these do taste like

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:26.850
elaichi, which is cardamom, and ginger.

00:16:26.850 --> 00:16:29.377
Yeah, they don't quite have the soul

00:16:29.377 --> 00:16:31.470
of a chai that you get on the roadside,

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:34.620
but I really love how
Dunkin' has tried to do this.

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:36.120
Makes you feel a little bit more at home,

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:38.370
so thank you, Dunkin'.

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:42.750
Sandwiches, and wraps, and
bagels, and breakfast stuff.

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:44.460
Oh. My.

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:45.840
Get a good look, India.

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:47.820
We have a huge selection

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:51.240
of non-doughnut-y breakfast sandwiches,

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:52.890
variety stuff you can get.

00:16:52.890 --> 00:16:55.203
Oh, man, I hit a wall, and I apologize.

00:16:56.970 --> 00:16:57.803
And I'm back.

00:16:57.803 --> 00:17:01.560
You can get yourself maple
sugar bacon breakfast sandwich.

00:17:01.560 --> 00:17:05.310
We have these Wake-Up Wraps,
and Wake-Up Wraps are,

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:08.370
I don't know, really
phoned-in breakfast tacos.

00:17:08.370 --> 00:17:09.780
I don't know how else to describe it.

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:12.330
It's a tortilla. They put
the stuff they already had

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:13.590
for the other sandwiches in there.

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:14.670
They fold it over.

00:17:14.670 --> 00:17:16.380
I'll just grab one. You
can get yourself one,

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:18.393
and oh, man, this thing is like ...

00:17:20.483 --> 00:17:21.316
[glass shattering]

00:17:21.316 --> 00:17:23.238
Hey, everyone watching this video,

00:17:23.238 --> 00:17:24.771
in the comments, let me know:

00:17:24.771 --> 00:17:27.454
I show you this, and then when I open it,

00:17:27.454 --> 00:17:29.820
are you more likely to
eat this or less likely?

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:31.200
Let me know in the comments.

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:32.940
Dunkin', nobody wants these.

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:36.750
You can get yourself a
tomato pesto grilled cheese.

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:39.292
Pesto's fine and all, but
when something has pesto on it

00:17:39.292 --> 00:17:40.650
and you don't realize it,
doesn't this look like --

00:17:40.650 --> 00:17:42.600
like, look at this green.
Does that look like,

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:43.650
would you go, "Oh, it's pesto,"

00:17:43.650 --> 00:17:45.270
or would you be like, "Ugh,
I think that's moldy"?

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:46.450
Also got the grilled cheese.

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:48.422
Oh!

00:17:48.422 --> 00:17:51.420
[gavel thuds]

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:54.240
Then you get yourself a
sourdough breakfast sandwich.

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:57.630
Yo, these things solidified.

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:59.430
Probably edible a few hours ago.

00:17:59.430 --> 00:18:00.690
I'll take a bite of this.

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:02.263
Sausage, egg, and cheese.

00:18:03.939 --> 00:18:05.577
Yeah, not bad.

00:18:05.577 --> 00:18:06.660
Bacon, egg, and cheese.

00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:09.270
Somewhere encased in this
melted cheese is bacon,

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:10.103
I assure you.

00:18:10.103 --> 00:18:14.280
There's also a turkey sausage,
egg, and cheese somewhere.

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:18.540
Oh, you can also get bagels
at your Dunkin' Donuts.

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:19.830
Why? I don't know.

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:21.963
But you can get your bagels plain,

00:18:21.963 --> 00:18:24.704
cinnamon raisin, multigrain,

00:18:24.704 --> 00:18:28.140
sesame seed, and this one, everything.

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:29.755
And you can get yourself
some cream cheeses,

00:18:29.755 --> 00:18:33.720
including garden veggie,
strawberry, and plain.

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:35.400
Also you can get an avocado spread,

00:18:35.400 --> 00:18:36.960
which they did not include.

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:38.580
Dunkin'!

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:40.260
India, you're not gonna believe this.

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:43.500
Our Dunkin' Donuts, you
can get a side of, [laughs]

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:47.160
you can get a side of something
called snackin' bacon.

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:49.110
What's snackin' bacon, you ask?

00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:52.020
It is a bag of bacon.

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:53.430
Bagel minis.

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:55.170
You can get plain and everything bagels.

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:56.160
Here's one right now.

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:57.998
I think these have cream
cheese inside of them.

00:18:59.190 --> 00:19:00.023
Yeah.

00:19:01.170 --> 00:19:03.173
I don't think I've ever
had one of these before.

00:19:04.980 --> 00:19:06.300
That's not a bad idea.

00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:07.350
Not bad, guys.

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:10.050
Also in the US, you can get
an order of hash browns.

00:19:10.050 --> 00:19:13.200
Now, at Dunkin' Donuts,
apparently you can get these,

00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:14.100
what do we call these?

00:19:14.100 --> 00:19:15.622
Omelet bites?

00:19:15.622 --> 00:19:17.340
You get bacon, egg, and cheese

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:18.720
or egg white and veggie.

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:23.640
C'mon. This is straight
taken from Starbucks, right?

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:25.920
We went to the Dunkin' India
website, and over there,

00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:28.497
on the menu, they claim to sell burgers

00:19:28.497 --> 00:19:30.480
and a few sides, like nachos.

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:32.070
However, we went to the outlets,

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:33.780
and the managers said
that they're phasing out

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:36.540
all savory food in Dunkin' nationally.

00:19:36.540 --> 00:19:38.370
But he was kind enough to make us

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:40.830
one single non-veg burger,

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:43.260
just so that we get to taste
what it would've been like.

00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:45.330
It has a whole chicken piece in there,

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:46.470
which is already kind of nice.

00:19:46.470 --> 00:19:49.800
Some onions, what looks
like tandoori mayo,

00:19:49.800 --> 00:19:52.353
and the bun. Looks pretty tasty.

00:19:56.460 --> 00:19:57.781
Oh, my God.

00:19:58.860 --> 00:20:00.420
That's actually really good.

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:02.700
I've done many episodes of "Food Wars,"

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:04.470
tasted many burgers from restaurants

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:07.140
that are literally burger joints,

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:10.050
and this literally rivals those burgers.

00:20:10.050 --> 00:20:11.190
This is pretty good.

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:12.840
What's happening, Dunkin'?

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:15.390
OK, so, the fact is that
Dunkin' has actually

00:20:15.390 --> 00:20:17.820
scaled down massively here in India.

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:18.960
In Bengal, where we're filming,

00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:21.300
there used to be 20 Dunkin' Donut outlets.

00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:22.800
Now there are only three.

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:24.728
So rumor has it that Dunkin' might be

00:20:24.728 --> 00:20:26.958
phasing out of India in general,

00:20:26.958 --> 00:20:29.850
and the decision is going to
be made in the coming weeks.

00:20:29.850 --> 00:20:32.550
So maybe this video is
the last remaining legacy

00:20:32.550 --> 00:20:34.020
of Dunkin' in India.

00:20:34.020 --> 00:20:38.040
And this is probably the last
burger that is ever eaten.

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:39.540
Oh, dude, this might be the --

00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:42.480
guys, this might be the
last burger ever consumed

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:44.388
from Dunkin' Donuts here in India.

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:48.660
OK, let's talk price.

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:51.810
This large Americano is rupees 139,

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:54.360
which is currently $1.71.

00:20:54.360 --> 00:20:56.250
But keep in mind, at the
time that we're filming this,

00:20:56.250 --> 00:20:58.800
the Indian rupee is at an all-time low,

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:00.210
so hopefully things will get better

00:21:00.210 --> 00:21:02.490
and this won't cost so much.

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:06.090
That same drink in the US is $3.69,

00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:09.490
or 293.44 rupees.

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:13.320
That's a 63.9% increase in price.

00:21:13.320 --> 00:21:15.720
OK, so the biggest menu item
that we have here in India

00:21:15.720 --> 00:21:17.160
is our box of six.

00:21:17.160 --> 00:21:18.451
Now, you can get two categories.

00:21:18.451 --> 00:21:20.984
You can get classic doughnuts,
which are a lot simpler,

00:21:20.984 --> 00:21:23.220
and it'll cost you rupees 399.

00:21:23.220 --> 00:21:24.917
Or you can get the favorites doughnuts,

00:21:24.917 --> 00:21:27.330
which we have here, which
are a lot more extravagant

00:21:27.330 --> 00:21:29.730
and will cost you rupees 499,

00:21:29.730 --> 00:21:32.550
which amounts to USD 6.12 right now.

00:21:32.550 --> 00:21:36.120
If you want 12 doughnuts, you
need to get two boxes of six,

00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:39.120
which will cost you rupees 998.

00:21:39.120 --> 00:21:43.477
For food, our biggest menu
item is a dozen doughnuts.

00:21:43.477 --> 00:21:45.152
$18.73,

00:21:45.152 --> 00:21:49.927
or 1,492.85 rupees.

00:21:49.927 --> 00:21:51.240
Thank you.

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:54.540
Our biggest drink is
the Box O' Joe Avella.

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:56.557
It's the most expensive single menu item.

00:21:56.557 --> 00:21:58.307
$27.48,

00:21:58.307 --> 00:22:02.248
or 2,190.25 rupees.

00:22:02.248 --> 00:22:04.230
Now, in India we have
something called a vada,

00:22:04.230 --> 00:22:06.846
which is pretty much a doughnut,

00:22:06.846 --> 00:22:08.671
but it's savory and it's fried.

00:22:08.671 --> 00:22:10.950
And I want to say that
those cost around 20 rupees,

00:22:10.950 --> 00:22:12.720
while this original glazed

00:22:12.720 --> 00:22:14.470
that I've bitten into a few times

00:22:14.470 --> 00:22:16.170
costs 85 rupees.

00:22:16.170 --> 00:22:19.230
So, it's important to know
this price difference,

00:22:19.230 --> 00:22:21.600
and people here will
definitely think about that

00:22:21.600 --> 00:22:23.300
before buying something like this.

00:22:27.510 --> 00:22:29.553
Nikhil, stop eating the props!

00:22:32.040 --> 00:22:34.380
OK, so Dunkin' Donuts
India has not released

00:22:34.380 --> 00:22:36.780
any of their nutritional
info out for the public.

00:22:36.780 --> 00:22:38.142
And they've not gotten back to us

00:22:38.142 --> 00:22:40.650
when we asked them for
information, as of now.

00:22:40.650 --> 00:22:43.015
However, I can confirm that one doughnut

00:22:43.015 --> 00:22:45.655
is probably less
nutritious than one salad.

00:22:47.130 --> 00:22:49.230
Let's talk about Dunkin' US nutrition,

00:22:49.230 --> 00:22:50.700
starting with the glazed doughnut.

00:22:50.700 --> 00:22:53.350
In the US, it has 360 calories,

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:54.720
22 grams of fat,

00:22:54.720 --> 00:22:56.403
10 grams of saturated fat,

00:22:56.403 --> 00:22:58.770
420 milligrams of sodium --

00:22:58.770 --> 00:22:59.790
420.

00:22:59.790 --> 00:23:01.440
39 grams of carbs,

00:23:01.440 --> 00:23:03.456
and 18 grams of sugar.

00:23:03.456 --> 00:23:06.360
And let's compare that
doughnut to this one,

00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:07.530
the Boston cream.

00:23:07.530 --> 00:23:11.430
In the USA, a Boston
cream is 270 calories,

00:23:11.430 --> 00:23:12.654
11 grams of fat,

00:23:12.654 --> 00:23:14.970
320 milligrams of sodium,

00:23:14.970 --> 00:23:16.003
39 grams of carbs,

00:23:16.003 --> 00:23:18.003
and 18 grams of sugar.

00:23:18.003 --> 00:23:20.850
Dunkin' Donuts large iced
Dunkin' dark-roast coffee

00:23:20.850 --> 00:23:22.920
with cream and sugar, in the US,

00:23:22.920 --> 00:23:24.986
is 260 calories,

00:23:24.986 --> 00:23:26.261
12 grams of fat,

00:23:26.261 --> 00:23:28.290
and 37 grams of carbs.

00:23:28.290 --> 00:23:29.962
Now, assuming that the iced coffee

00:23:29.962 --> 00:23:31.928
is the same in the US and India,

00:23:31.928 --> 00:23:34.878
getting a large iced
coffee with cream and sugar

00:23:34.878 --> 00:23:37.362
and both the glazed and
a Boston cream doughnut

00:23:37.362 --> 00:23:39.540
is 890 calories.

00:23:39.540 --> 00:23:44.070
That's 35.6% of your daily calorie intake.

00:23:44.070 --> 00:23:45.078
Yo.

00:23:47.610 --> 00:23:49.230
Again, Dunkin' Donuts has not released

00:23:49.230 --> 00:23:51.540
any of their ingredients to the public.

00:23:51.540 --> 00:23:53.250
However, there is one huge difference

00:23:53.250 --> 00:23:54.980
between the US and Indian doughnuts,

00:23:54.980 --> 00:23:58.470
and that is that the Indian
doughnuts are all eggless.

00:23:58.470 --> 00:24:01.200
This is because a huge percentage
of Indians are vegetarian,

00:24:01.200 --> 00:24:04.410
especially Hindus, and so
they even consider eating egg

00:24:04.410 --> 00:24:06.690
as non-veg food, and so, yeah.

00:24:06.690 --> 00:24:09.540
Most fast-food restaurants
have decided to not use egg

00:24:09.540 --> 00:24:12.120
in any of their foods to
make it more accessible

00:24:12.120 --> 00:24:13.680
to a larger part of India.

00:24:13.680 --> 00:24:15.720
But the US does have it on its site,

00:24:15.720 --> 00:24:17.820
so we'll share with you
the ingredients right now.

00:24:17.820 --> 00:24:18.990
First up, the coffee.

00:24:18.990 --> 00:24:21.090
Regardless of getting it hot or cold,

00:24:21.090 --> 00:24:25.860
if you get it black, it's going
to be 100% arabica coffee.

00:24:25.860 --> 00:24:27.060
Nice. Now,

00:24:27.060 --> 00:24:28.830
if you want to add cream and sugar to it,

00:24:28.830 --> 00:24:31.020
then you are adding milk, cream,

00:24:31.020 --> 00:24:32.940
disodium phosphate as a stabilizer,

00:24:32.940 --> 00:24:36.090
sodium citrate as a stabilizer, and sugar.

00:24:36.090 --> 00:24:38.250
If you're going to be adding
flavor to your coffee drink,

00:24:38.250 --> 00:24:41.490
one flavor you can get in both
India and the US is caramel.

00:24:41.490 --> 00:24:45.363
And in the US, our caramel
flavor is made up of all this.

00:24:46.340 --> 00:24:48.270
In the US, our standard glazed doughnut

00:24:48.270 --> 00:24:50.613
is made up of all of these things.

00:24:51.780 --> 00:24:53.317
You think that's a lot?

00:24:53.317 --> 00:24:55.869
Here's everything in our
Boston cream doughnuts.

00:24:55.869 --> 00:24:59.250
Yikes, that's a lot of words.

